# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user

# Secrets. None of these may ever be committed: the .p8 can push notifications
# to every device the app is installed on until it is revoked, and .env holds
# the account password.
#
# keys/ is named explicitly as well as by extension. *.p8 already covers the
# file, but a directory that exists to hold secrets should say so in here --
# the next thing dropped in it may not be a .p8.
.env
secrets/
keys/
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Learned history. This contains REAL ROUTE COORDINATES -- a few miles of turns
# can be matched against a road network and put back on the map, and it is a
# child's daily route to and from school. Keep it local: never commit it, never
# attach it to a bug report, never upload it to a service.
data/
*history*.json
wtb-arrivals.json

# macOS / Xcode
.DS_Store
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/

# Native build output (the xcframework is regenerated by scripts/build-ios-native.sh)
ios/build/

# Generated by XcodeGen from ios/project.yml. The spec is the source of truth;
# committing the project file too would give two things to keep in step, and the
# .pbxproj is the one nobody can review.
ios/*.xcodeproj/
